{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FzE9vQznTdkwdgna6rZsRT","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\tImplement user-service\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\txlight05\nlabels:\tasdlc, implementation, pending\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\tmekanamwedakarannaone3 (In Progress)\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t1\n--\n## Component Constraints\n- **Name:** user-service\n- **Type:** service\n- **Language/Stack:** Go\n- **App Path (within repo):** `/user-service`\n\n## Responsibilities\n- Provide user profile management and retrieval\n- Track manager-employee reporting relationships\n- Expose user context (whether user is employee or manager)\n- Provide health check endpoint for service monitoring\n- Store and serve employee and manager data\n- Enable querying of direct reports for any manager\n\n## Key Considerations\n- Use in-memory storage for simplicity with initial seed data\n- Implement proper error handling for missing users (404 responses)\n- Ensure manager relationships are bidirectional (managerId on employee, reports queryable from manager)\n- Log all requests for observability\n- Follow the OpenAPI specification exactly for request/response formats\n- Service must be containerizable and listen on port 9090\n\n## Project Structure Requirements\nCreate a production-ready project structure in the current directory:\n- go.mod with proper module path\n- cmd/ or main.go entry point\n- Dockerfile (multi-stage build)\n- Internal packages as needed (handlers/, services/, models/)\n\nCreate a `workload.yaml` at the root of your component directory to declare endpoints and dependencies. Refer to the OpenChoreo workload configuration guidance in your skill for the correct format, endpoint types, dependency wiring, and the SPA nginx proxy pattern for frontend components.\n\nThe platform will handle git commit, push, build, and deploy automatically.\n## OpenAPI Spec\n\n```yaml\nopenapi: 3.0.3\ninfo:\n  title: User Service API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: Manages employee profiles, manager relationships, and user context\npaths:\n  /health:\n    get:\n      summary: Health check\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Service is healthy\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  status:\n                    type: string\n                    example: ok\n  /users/{userId}:\n    get:\n      summary: Get user profile\n      parameters:\n        - name: userId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: User profile\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/User'\n        '404':\n          description: User not found\n  /users/{userId}/manager:\n    get:\n      summary: Get the manager of a user\n      parameters:\n        - name: userId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Manager details\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/User'\n        '404':\n          description: Manager not found\n  /users/{userId}/reports:\n    get:\n      summary: Get direct reports for a manager\n      parameters:\n        - name: userId\n          in: path\n          required: true\n          schema:\n            type: string\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: List of direct reports\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: array\n                items:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/User'\ncomponents:\n  schemas:\n    User:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: string\n        name:\n          type: string\n        email:\n          type: string\n        managerId:\n          type: string\n          nullable: true\n        isManager:\n          type: boolean\n```\n\n## Agent Instructions\nImplement a Go HTTP service on port 9090 that manages employee profiles and manager relationships. Use net/http for the server and in-memory storage (map) for user data. Seed with at least 5 employees and 2 managers, where each user has: id (string), name, email, managerId (nullable string), and isManager (boolean). Implement GET /health returning {\"status\":\"ok\"}, GET /users/{userId} returning user object or 404, GET /users/{userId}/manager returning the manager object or 404 if no manager exists, and GET /users/{userId}/reports returning array of users whose managerId matches the userId. All responses use JSON. Log all incoming requests with method and path. Handle invalid userIds with 404 responses.\n\n## General Constraints\n- Write ALL files in the current working directory (do NOT create files outside it).\n- The component must have a Dockerfile for containerized builds.\n- Implement the full API contract from the task — every endpoint must be functional.\n- Use the dependencies listed to understand what other services this component talks to.\n- The app MUST start without any required environment variables — use sensible hardcoded defaults for all config (JWT secrets, DB paths, API URLs, etc.). Environment variables may override defaults but must never be required.\n- Do NOT stub or mock — write real, working implementations.\n- Do NOT run, start, or execute the application server locally. Only write source files. The platform builds and deploys your code automatically — local execution is unnecessary and will cause port conflicts.\n- If you must run a quick compile check (e.g. `go build`, `tsc --noEmit`), do so without starting a server. Never use `go run`, `npm start`, `node server.js`, or any command that starts a long-running process.\n\n## Working Directory\nAll file operations must happen inside this directory:\n\n```\n/Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone3/user-service\n```\n\nBefore you do anything else, navigate there:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/senith/.asdlc/repos/default/mekanamwedakarannaone3/user-service\n```\n\nDo NOT create files outside this directory. Do NOT `cd` elsewhere during your work.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73760c50-4928-40a1-b6dc-5546dd6d2855","uuid":"41fa81e1-19e1-495c-a122-bec769e32fdc","timestamp":"2026-05-02T20:00:20.724Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"title:\tImplement user-service\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\txlight05\nlabels:\tasdlc, implementation, pending\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\tmekanamwedakarannaone3 (In Progress)\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t1\n--\n## Component Constraints\n- **Name:** user-service\n- **Type:** service\n- **Language/Stack:** Go\n- **App Path (within repo):** `/user-service`\n\n## Responsibilities\n- Provide user profile management and retrieval\n- Track manager-employee reporting relationships\n- Expose user context (whether user is employee or manager)\n- Provide health check endpoint for service monitoring\n- Store and serve employee and manager data\n- Enable querying of direct reports for any manager\n\n## Key Considerations\n- Use in-memory storage for simplicity with initial seed data\n- Implement proper error handling for missing users (404 responses)\n- Ensure manager relationships are bidirectional (managerId on employee, reports queryable from manager)\n- Log all requests for observability\n- Follow the OpenAPI specification exactly for request/response formats\n- Service must be containerizable and listen on port 9090\n\n## Project Structure Requirements\nCreate a production-ready project structure in the current directory:\n- go.mod with proper module path\n- cmd/ or main.go entry point\n- Dockerfile (multi-stage build)\n- Internal packages as needed (handlers/, services/, models/)\n\nCreate a `workload.yaml` at the root